  "merger_description": "Vertex Pharmaceuticals Incorporated (**Vertex**) proposes to acquire 100% of the issued shares in Crinetics Pharmaceuticals, Inc. (**Crinetics**) (the **Acquisition**).\n\nVertex is a US-based biotechnology company, listed on the Nasdaq Global Select Market under the symbol \u201cVRTX\u201d, that develops, manufactures and markets a range of pharmaceutical products for serious diseases. It currently has 7 approved products for the treatment of cystic fibrosis, sickle cell disease, transfusion dependent beta thalassemia, and acute pain (including 5 that are approved by the Therapeutic Goods Administration (TGA) and supplied in Australia). It also has certain products currently in development stages for other serious diseases.\n\nCrinetics is a US-based pharmaceutical company, listed on the Nasdaq Global Select Market under the ticker symbol \u201cCRNX\u201d, that has a focus on discovering, developing, and commercialising treatments for endocrine diseases. Crinetics has one product on market in the US, Palsonify (paltusotine), a prescription oral medication used to treat acromegaly, a rare hormonal disorder. Palsonify is not currently approved or under review for approval by the TGA for supply in Australia. Crinetics also has a range of products currently in development stages in the endocrinology, endocrine-driven oncology and metabolic diseases spaces.",
